/**

This function checks the timestamp of each file enlisted in the <code>ejbFiles</code>
and contrasts them with the timestamp of the <code>jarFile</code>.
If the timestamp of the <code>jarFile</code> surpasses that of every EJB file,
it yields a positive result in the form of <code>true</code>;
otherwise, it yields <code>false</code>.
TODO: Identify an approach to inspect the convention-named manifest file.
@param ejbFiles Hash table encompassing EJB classes (and other) files, destined for
css
            addition to the finalized JAR file
@param jarFile JAR file set to contain all EJB classes (and other) files
@return A boolean denoting whether the <code>jarFile</code> is up to date
*/

