/**

Derive the "intno" of the provided Message. <p>
If the predecessor of the given message possesses only one successor,
then the string representation of the provided integer is returned. <p>
If the predecessor of the given message has multiple successors, then
it denotes concurrent message execution, such as Message 3.1a and Message 3.1b
occurring in parallel within activation 3.1. In such cases, a syntax like: 1a, 1b, 1c is employed.
This implies that the initial successor in the ordered succession list
with multiple entries will be assigned the suffix "a", the second "b", and so forth.
TODO: Outline any exceptional behavior in the documentation.
@param umlMessage the UML message object for which to generate the sequence number
@param umlPredecessor the immediate predecessor message (UML object) having the given message as a successor
@param position the integer position of the given message within its sequence
@return the generated sequence expression string,
or null if the given Message was null
*/

/**

Produce the "intno" corresponding to the provided Message. <p>
If the predecessor of the given message has only one successor, then the string representation of the provided integer is returned. <p>
If the predecessor of the given message has multiple successors, then this signifies parallel message execution, such as Message 3.1a and Message 3.1b running concurrently within activation 3.1.
Consequently, a syntax like: 1a, 1b, 1c is utilized.
This implies that the initial successor in the ordered succession list with multiple entries will receive the postfix "a", the second "b", and so on.
TODO: Specify any exceptional behavior in the documentation.
@param umlMessage the UML message object for which the sequence number is generated
@param umlPredecessor the immediate predecessor message (UML object) that has the given message as a successor
@param position the integer position of the given message within its sequence
@return the generated sequence expression string,
or null if the given Message was null
*/

/**

Compute the "intno" for the given Message. <p>
